 of nutritional supplements.", "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT:Nutritional support encompasses a range of interventions designed to enhance dietary intake and improve health outcomes for patients. This practice includes the use of oral nutritional supplements and other dietary interventions aimed at managing health conditions and improving nutritional status. It is particularly important for patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through regular eating, such as those with complications from conditions like obesity or diabetes. Overall, nutritional support plays a crucial role in providing dietary assistance to individuals in need, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery.", "HYPERPROTEIC NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENT:", "MARÍA D. BALLESTEROS POMAR:María D. Ballesteros Pomar is a medical specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, and the coordinator of the Nutrition Area of the SEEN at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario de León.", "SEEN:The SEEN is the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition, focusing on diabetes and nutrition-related health issues.", "CASTILLA Y LEÓN:Castilla y León is an autonomous community in Spain that is experiencing a notable increase in the prevalence of diabetes and related mortality rates. This region is characterized by an aging population, which contributes to the growing health concern surrounding diabetes. In response to this public health issue, clinical case conferences have been held in Castilla y León to address and discuss the challenges posed by diabetes in the community. Overall, diabetes remains a significant health concern in Castilla y León, highlighting the need for ongoing attention and intervention.", "IDF:The International Diabetes Federation (IDF) is an organization dedicated to providing data and advocacy related to diabetes on a global scale. It plays a crucial role in raising awareness and promoting education about diabetes through its various initiatives. One of its 